Description: Create tile bitmaps premultiplied for fast drawing
 Tiles are created with createImageBitmap(..., { premultiplyAlpha:
 'none' }). Chromium 102, used by Debian Bookworm's QtWebEngine 6.4,
 cannot keep such unpremultiplied bitmaps on the GPU, so every
 drawImage() of a tile converts and re-uploads it (about 5 ms per
 256x256 tile vs. 0.04 ms for a premultiplied bitmap). This made
 scrolling and repainting very slow: drawImage took ~85% of the
 renderer main thread time.
 .
 Tile bitmaps are only drawn with 2D canvas drawImage(), for which a
 bitmap premultiplied at creation gives the same result as an
 unpremultiplied one premultiplied at draw time, so use 'premultiply'.
Author: Puavo Org <dev@opinsys.fi>
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/online/browser/src/app/TilesMiddleware.ts
+++ b/online/browser/src/app/TilesMiddleware.ts
@@ -521,7 +521,10 @@
 			const image = new ImageData(clampedData, this.tileSize, this.tileSize);
 			bitmaps.push(
 				createImageBitmap(image, {
-					premultiplyAlpha: 'none',
+					// Not 'none': Chromium 102 (QtWebEngine 6.4 in Debian Bookworm)
+					// re-uploads unpremultiplied bitmaps on every drawImage, making
+					// tile painting ~100x slower. Same result for 2D drawImage.
+					premultiplyAlpha: 'premultiply',
 				}),
 			);
 			deltas.push(delta);
--- a/online/browser/src/layer/tile/CanvasTileWorkerSrc.js
+++ b/online/browser/src/layer/tile/CanvasTileWorkerSrc.js
@@ -86,7 +86,10 @@
 					);
 					bitmaps.push(
 						createImageBitmap(image, {
-							premultiplyAlpha: 'none',
+							// Not 'none': Chromium 102 (QtWebEngine 6.4 in Debian Bookworm)
+							// re-uploads unpremultiplied bitmaps on every drawImage, making
+							// tile painting ~100x slower. Same result for 2D drawImage.
+							premultiplyAlpha: 'premultiply',
 						}),
 					);
 					tilesWithBitmaps.push(tile);
